# Generated from: specs/383-reject-missing-near-miss-or-duplicate-delivery-file-declarations/requirements.md
Feature: Require one canonical File(s) declaration per delivery task
  Approved delivery tasks must not silently lose or combine publication authority.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Missing declaration is rejected before dispatch
    Given an Approved spec with an admitted task that has no File(s) declaration
    When execute performs publication scope preflight
    Then publication_scope_unproven identifies the spec and task
    And no pane, worker, or bind subprocess is created

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Near-miss Files label is rejected before dispatch
    Given an Approved spec with an admitted task declaring Files instead of File(s)
    When execute performs publication scope preflight
    Then publication_scope_unproven identifies the near-miss line and task
    And no pane, worker, or bind subprocess is created

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Duplicate canonical declarations are rejected before dispatch
    Given an Approved spec with two File(s) declarations in one admitted task
    When execute performs publication scope preflight
    Then publication_scope_unproven identifies the duplicate line and task
    And no declaration authority is combined

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Valid tasks retain bounded authority
    Given every admitted task has one canonical File(s) declaration
    When publication scope is bound
    Then the allowed paths contain declared and spec-owned paths only
    And non-admitted task metadata grants no authority

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Publication and authoring enforce the same invariant
    Given write-spec is producing an Approved tasks.md
    When publication validation evaluates the package
    Then each admitted task must have exactly one canonical File(s) declaration
    And missing, near-miss, and duplicate declarations use the located publication_scope_unproven contract
